    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) anchor our offensive production. **Seiya Suzuki** draws a favorable matchup against Abbott, who carries a shaky 4.89 xERA, allowing **Seiya Suzuki** to leverage a 19% boost in SP skill efficiency and a batting order prime for counting stats. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits from a confluence of positive factors, including a 16% park adjustment and a 14% platoon edge against Baz. We are also leaning heavily into the speed-first profile of **Mickey Moniak** (69.68), who is an auto-start today due to the 88% stolen base success rate allowed by the opposing battery, which significantly mitigates his raw park penalty.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Austin Riley**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 46.08 efficiency rating. While his talent profile is undeniable, his performance today is hampered by a double-whammy of a pitcher's park and a significant wind-in factor, ultimately causing him to fall behind **Kyle Karros** (46.17) in our model. We are playing it cautious with **Brice Turang** (47.02) despite his high batting order position; he faces a formidable arm in Skenes, and his score is depressed by a 19% SP skill penalty and a league-best catcher pop-time that makes his aggressive base-running approach a high-risk proposition.\n\nBeyond the baseline projections, we are keeping a close eye on **Edwin Arroyo** (40.01), who sits right on the edge of our efficiency floor. His value is buoyed by his switch-hitting ability, but his spot at the bottom of the order forces him into the \"marginal\" start category. We have successfully bypassed the risks associated with starting **Zach McKinstry** (35.92) or **Cole Young** (37.13), as both failed to clear the 40-point threshold against their respective tough matchups today. With the team sitting at a competitive inflection point, our lineup focuses on maximizing favorable platoon splits and exploiting the exploitable mechanics of opposing pitchers.",
